3:  *
4:  * One worker `explore` call = one bounded, read-only session with a FRESH context window. A resident-only selector may
5:  * route it to a smaller empirically tool-capable model; otherwise it uses the worker unchanged. Owns the per-session
6:  * query budget; every degraded path resolves to null so exploration never
7:  * blocks the worker (the tool tells it to fall back to its own retrieval).
