1: /**
2:  * Rich descriptors for the currently-LOADED LM Studio models, read from the NATIVE `/api/v1/models` endpoint when
3:  * available, with a minimal `/api/v0/models` fallback for LM Studio builds that do not expose the rich endpoint. Crucially this
4:  * separates the two identifiers LM Studio carries:
5:  *
6:  *   - `loaded_instances[].id` — the **runtime id you INVOKE**, i.e. the user's per-instance ALIAS (e.g.
7:  *     `qwen3.5-9b-mtp-q4-k-xl-laptop`, a name the user gave the instance to mark which machine it's on);
8:  *   - `key` — the **real publisher model key** (e.g. `qwen3.5-9b-mtp`), the right string to match against the §5.AL
9:  *     catalog / llmfit DB. (User, 2026-07-01: "get the real model names from the API, then use those.")
10:  *
11:  * It also surfaces the per-model card facts the runtime can use as EMPIRICAL capability ground truth (the §5.AB vision —
12:  * "based on empirical information it collects by itself on runtime"): `type` (`llm` vs `embedding` — an authoritative
13:  * embedding filter, not a name guess), `capabilities.trained_for_tool_use`, a declared `reasoning` capability, and the
14:  * `architecture` family. Read-only GET — never triggers a load (the no-load directive, see `lmstudio-loaded-models.ts`).
15:  *
16:  * Pure parser + injectable fetch, so it is unit-testable without a live endpoint.
17:  */
