2:  * F11.2h in-repo few-shot exemplar injection (CEDAR-style, deterministic retrieval).
3:  *
4:  * The cheapest way to make a small model write code that LOOKS NATIVE is to show it 1–2 similar existing
5:  * functions from this repo as style/API exemplars — retrieval-augmented few-shot beats fine-tuning at ~2 shots
6:  * (CEDAR ICSE'23). This module retrieves them WITHOUT a model: candidate = every named, exemplar-sized function
7:  * declaration; similarity = function-identity/path token overlap with the task text (camelCase-aware); the card's own target
8:  * files are excluded (the worker already reads those). Rendering is prompt-ready and honestly labeled as style
9:  * reference, not instruction. Activation is OPT-IN (`NKLEIN_FEWSHOT_EXEMPLARS`) until a fleet A/B proves the
