2:  * F12.81 ledger-sourced dynamic few-shot injection — PURE core.
3:  *
4:  * The single biggest measured lever for small-model tool use is a few CONCRETE examples of the tool-calling shape
5:  * you want (Haiku 11%→75% with three), and two details matter: examples must be real MESSAGE turns rather than a
6:  * string blob, and they must be selected PER CARD rather than fixed. This is DSPy's BootstrapFewShot idea over
7:  * !Klein's own passing traces: retrieve the most similar SUCCESSFUL past attempts and replay them as ChatML.
8:  *
9:  * Distinct from F11.2h, which retrieves in-repo code exemplars — this retrieves *behavioural* exemplars (how a
10:  * past card was actually driven to success).
11:  *
12:  * Scope note: the attempt ledger stores no card TEXT, so the caller joins ledger attempts to their board titles
13:  * and passes candidates in. Selection, similarity and formatting live here; the join stays with the caller.
14:  *
15:  * Honesty stance: only SUCCESSFUL attempts are ever offered as exemplars, an attempt with no tool calls teaches
16:  * nothing about tool use and is skipped, and a card with no similar history yields NO messages — an irrelevant
17:  * example is worse than none, because a small model will imitate it.
18:  */
19: 
20: export interface ExemplarCandidate {
21: 	readonly attemptId: string;
